Provides: update-notifier
Description: Patrone Linux's desktop
 Ubuntu's desktop with Patrone's branding and apps, and nothing that reports
 to Canonical: no whoopsie (error reports), ubuntu-insights or ubuntu-report
 (system reports), and no apport-gtk, the crash dialog that offered to send
 them. Crash reports still collect in /var/crash for debugging, and nothing
 sends them. First-login setup skips Ubuntu's page that asks to send reports
 and its Ubuntu Pro page, and Ubuntu Pro's apt news and ESM check run only on
 a machine attached to Ubuntu Pro. Ubuntu Pro's notice at login
 (update-notifier, whose place in Ubuntu's desktop this package takes) and
 its desktop service (ubuntu-advantage-desktop-daemon) are removed; Patrone
 Software tells of updates.
 .
 The clock is set from NTS servers run by Cloudflare, Netnod, PTB and SIDN
 Labs, NetworkManager checks for Wi-Fi sign-in pages with GNOME's server, and
 nothing offers to upgrade to Ubuntu's next release. Its app store is GNOME
 Software, with Patrone's picks, in place of Canonical's App Center.
 .
 It also brings a few everyday tools: fastfetch (system information, in
 Patrone's colors), nano and the full vim; btop and htop (what's running);
 tree, ripgrep (rg) and fzf (finding files and text); bat (files with
 highlighting, run as batcat); ncdu (what's using the disk); and 7zip (7z).
